        "text": "**(E)** is the true expression.\n\nIn its first part, \u201cthe capital of Nepal is Pokhara\u201d is false, so the `not` applied to that conjunction is true. But the other factor is false: both \\(2(-6)>-9\\) and `not not not (6 - (-5 / -10) > 3)` are false. Thus the first part is false.\n\nIn the second part, \\(-7-(-2/-6)>-8\\) is true, making the inner `or` true. Its three preceding `not`s make it false, so the conjunction is false. The three `not`s outside that conjunction then make the second part **true**.\n\nTherefore, (E) is `false or true`, which evaluates to **true**.",
